From: BMC firmware
Subject: cmm: empty the forward engine when the daemon stops

A daemon that gets SIGTERM closed its sockets and left every connection
and bridged flow in the forward engine. Nothing removes them after that:
the engine keeps forwarding connections that have ended or whose route
changed, and "stop the daemon" does not turn fast forwarding off.

On SIGTERM, refuse new connections, then reset the forward engine while
the worker threads still run. Bridged flows are now refused as well while
fast forwarding is off; before, only conntrack events were. The reset
makes open connections continue through the stack, so
nf_conntrack_tcp_be_liberal is no longer set back to 0 on exit: strict
window checking would break every TCP connection that comes back.

The conntrack entries of those connections keep IPS_PERMANENT. Clearing
it here would let the kernel expire a connection at once whose timeout
ran out while the engine carried it.

---
--- a/cmm/src/cmm.c
+++ b/cmm/src/cmm.c
@@ -272,6 +272,16 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "%s: entered\n", __func__);
+
+	/*
+	 * Leave nothing in the forward engine: with the daemon gone, nobody
+	 * removes a connection that ended or whose route changed, and the
+	 * engine would keep forwarding it. The other threads still run, so
+	 * new connections are refused first; cmmFeReset() waits for the locks
+	 * they hold, which this thread never holds while it sits in pause().
+	 */
+	globalConf.enable = 0;
+	cmmFeReset(globalConf.cli.fci_handle);
 
 	cmmCliExit(&globalConf.cli);
 
--- a/cmm/src/conntrack.c
+++ b/cmm/src/conntrack.c
@@ -2599,7 +2599,13 @@
 {
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "%s:\n", __func__);
 
-	file_write(TCP_BE_LIBERAL_PATH, "0", 1);
+	/*
+	 * nf_conntrack_tcp_be_liberal stays 1. The connections the forward
+	 * engine carried go on through the stack once the daemon is gone,
+	 * and the kernel last saw their sequence numbers before they were
+	 * offloaded: with strict window checking their packets are INVALID,
+	 * are not translated by NAT any more, and the connections break.
+	 */
 }
 
 
--- a/cmm/src/module_rx.c
+++ b/cmm/src/module_rx.c
@@ -146,6 +146,13 @@
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "%s\n", __func__);
 	cmm_l2flow_print(DEBUG_INFO, l2flow_tmp, 0);
 
+	/* Fast forwarding is switched off (set activate 0, or the daemon is
+	 * stopping): the flow stays with the bridge, as a routed connection
+	 * stays with the stack. No answer is sent, so the bridge module
+	 * offers the flow again and a daemon that is active later takes it. */
+	if (!globalConf.enable)
+		return 0;
+
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "Input itf idx = %d ", iifi_idx);
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "Output itf idx = %d ", oifi_idx);
 	cmm_print(DEBUG_INFO, "Mark = %0x4\n", mark);
